  <section class="cell" id="download">
    <div class="cell-label">Setup</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="index-badge">00</span>Download the Dataset</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Pull Apple's full daily OHLCV history from Yahoo Finance and preview the raw frame.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">download.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">import yfinance as yf
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

plt.style.use("ggplot")
pd.set_option("display.max_columns", None)

# Download Apple historical stock prices
df = yf.download("AAPL", start="2018-01-01", end="2026-01-01")

df.head()</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="cleaning">
    <div class="cell-label">Data cleaning</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="index-badge">01</span>Data Cleaning</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Forward fill missing values, drop duplicates, normalise the date column, sort chronologically, and set the date as the index before saving to CSV.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">clean.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python"># Missing values
df.fillna(method='ffill', inplace=True)

# Remove duplicates
df.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)

# Convert Date
df.reset_index(inplace=True)
df['Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date'])

# Sort
df.sort_values("Date", inplace=True)

# Set Date Index
df.set_index("Date", inplace=True)

# Save the dataset
df.to_csv("aapl_stock.csv")</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q1">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 01</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> How has Apple's closing stock price changed over time?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Plots the full closing price series to reveal the long run trend.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">closing_price_trend.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">plt.figure(figsize=(14,6))
plt.plot(df.index, df['Close'])
plt.title('Apple Closing Price Trend')
plt.xlabel('Date')
plt.ylabel('Closing Price ($)')
plt.show()</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="output-note"><span class="tag">[out]</span> Chart renders once the notebook is executed against a live data pull.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q2">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 02</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> How has Apple's trading volume changed over time?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Traces daily volume to surface spikes around earnings, splits, and market events.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">volume_trend.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">plt.figure(figsize=(14,6))
plt.plot(df.index, df['Volume'])
plt.title('Trading Volume Trend')
plt.xlabel('Date')
plt.ylabel('Volume')
plt.show()</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="output-note"><span class="tag">[out]</span> Chart renders once the notebook is executed against a live data pull.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q3">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 03</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> How do the 7-day and 30-day moving averages compare with the closing price?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Engineers two rolling mean features and overlays them on the raw close price to show trend smoothing at different windows.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">moving_averages.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">df['MA7'] = df['Close'].rolling(window=7).mean()
df['MA30'] = df['Close'].rolling(window=30).mean()

plt.figure(figsize=(14,6))
plt.plot(df['Close'], label='Close Price')
plt.plot(df['MA7'], label='7-Day MA')
plt.plot(df['MA30'], label='30-Day MA')
plt.title('Moving Average Analysis')
plt.legend()
plt.show()</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="output-note"><span class="tag">[out]</span> Chart renders once the notebook is executed against a live data pull.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q4">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 04</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> What are the monthly returns, and how do they vary over time?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Resamples to month end closes and computes the percentage change month over month.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">monthly_returns.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">monthly_returns = df['Close'].resample('M').last().pct_change()

plt.figure(figsize=(14,6))
plt.plot(monthly_returns)
plt.title('Monthly Returns')
plt.xlabel('Month')
plt.ylabel('Return')
plt.show()</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="output-note"><span class="tag">[out]</span> Chart renders once the notebook is executed against a live data pull.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q5">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 05</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> Which stock features have the strongest relationships?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Correlation heatmap across all numeric columns (Open, High, Low, Close, Volume, and engineered features).</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">correlation_matrix.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">plt.figure(figsize=(10,8))
sns.heatmap(df.corr(numeric_only=True),
            annot=True,
            cmap='coolwarm',
            fmt='.2f')
plt.title('Correlation Matrix')
plt.show()</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="output-note"><span class="tag">[out]</span> Chart renders once the notebook is executed against a live data pull.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="cell" id="q6">
    <div class="cell-label">EDA · Question 06</div>
    <h2 class="q"><span class="qmark">Q.</span> What is the distribution of Apple's closing prices?</h2>
    <p class="narrative">Histogram of closing prices across the full date range.</p>
    <div class="code-card">
      <div class="bar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span class="filename">closing_price_distribution.py</span></div>
      <pre><code class="language-python">plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))
plt.hist(df['Close'], bins=30)
plt.title('Distribution of Closing Prices')
